Scenario: constructorInitializesTerminalView | Verifies that the TerminalView constructor initializes the view.
GIVEN a mocked controller.
WHEN a TerminalView is created.
THEN the view is not null.

Scenario: runCreatesFirstAccountAndEntersMainMenu | Verifies that the first account can be created successfully.
GIVEN no users exist and valid signup credentials are entered.
WHEN the view runs.
THEN the first account is created, the main menu is displayed, and the method returns 0.

Scenario: runReturnsOneWhenFirstAccountCreationFails | Verifies that signup failure prevents entry into the main menu.
GIVEN no users exist and the entered passwords do not match.
WHEN the view runs.
THEN account creation is attempted, the main menu is not displayed, and the method returns 1.

Scenario: runReturnsOneWhenSignupInputEnds | Verifies that the view handles signup input ending before account creation.
GIVEN no users exist and no signup input is provided.
WHEN the view runs.
THEN account creation is not attempted and the method returns 1.

Scenario: runLogsInExistingUser | Verifies that an existing user can log in successfully.
GIVEN an existing user enters valid login credentials.
WHEN the view runs.
THEN login succeeds, the main menu is displayed, and the output contains "Login successful."

Scenario: runRetriesAfterIncorrectLogin | Verifies that the view allows another login attempt after incorrect credentials.
GIVEN an existing user first enters an incorrect password and then a correct password.
WHEN the view runs.
THEN both login attempts are verified and the output contains "Incorrect username or password."

Scenario: runSetsUpPasswordForNewUser | Verifies that a user can set up their password when required.
GIVEN an existing user who needs to set up a password enters matching passwords.
WHEN the view runs.
THEN the password is changed and the main menu is displayed.

Scenario: runRetriesLoginWhenPasswordSetupFails | Verifies that the view returns to login after password setup fails.
GIVEN a user needs password setup and enters nonmatching passwords, followed by valid login credentials.
WHEN the view runs.
THEN password setup is attempted, login is retried, and the second login is verified.

Scenario: adminCanExitMainMenu | Verifies that an administrator can exit the main menu.
GIVEN an administrator successfully logs in and selects the exit option.
WHEN the view runs.
THEN the main menu is displayed and the method returns 0.

Scenario: regularUserCanExitMainMenu | Verifies that a regular user can exit the main menu.
GIVEN a regular user successfully logs in and selects the exit option.
WHEN the view runs.
THEN the main menu is displayed and the method returns 0.

Scenario: adminCanChangePassword | Verifies that an administrator can change their password.
GIVEN an administrator successfully logs in and enters matching new passwords.
WHEN the administrator selects the change-password option.
THEN the controller's changePassword method is called with the entered credentials.

Scenario: adminCanCreateUser | Verifies that an administrator can create another user.
GIVEN an administrator successfully logs in and enters a new username.
WHEN the administrator selects the create-user option.
THEN the controller's createUser method is called with the administrator's username and the new username.

Scenario: adminCanPromoteUser | Verifies that an administrator can promote another user.
GIVEN an administrator successfully logs in and enters "Promote bob".
WHEN the administrator selects the user-access management option.
THEN the controller's manageAccess method is called with "alice", "bob", and "Promote".

Scenario: adminCanDemoteUser | Verifies that an administrator can demote another user.
GIVEN an administrator successfully logs in and enters "Demote bob".
WHEN the administrator selects the user-access management option.
THEN the controller's manageAccess method is called with "alice", "bob", and "Demote".

Scenario: adminCanReviewAuditLog | Verifies that an administrator can review the audit log.
GIVEN an administrator successfully logs in.
WHEN the administrator selects the audit-log option.
THEN the controller's reviewAuditLog method is called with the administrator's username.

Scenario: adminCanReturnFromInvalidManageAccessInput | Verifies that invalid user-access input is handled before valid input is processed.
GIVEN an administrator enters invalid input followed by "Promote bob".
WHEN the administrator selects the user-access management option.
THEN the output contains "Invalid input." and the controller processes the valid promotion request.

Scenario: adminCanOpenBriefsMenu | Verifies that an administrator can open the briefs menu.
GIVEN an administrator successfully logs in.
WHEN the administrator selects the briefs option.
THEN the controller's browseMainMenu method is called with "alice" and "briefs".

Scenario: adminCanOpenAgentsMenu | Verifies that an administrator can open the agents menu.
GIVEN an administrator successfully logs in.
WHEN the administrator selects the agents option.
THEN the controller's browseMainMenu method is called with "alice" and "agents".

Scenario: adminCanOpenFacilitiesMenu | Verifies that an administrator can open the facilities menu.
GIVEN an administrator successfully logs in.
